<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian retail sales fall one pct in Dec.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian retail sales fall one pct in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian retail sales fell 1.0 percent to A$10.13 billion in December, seasonally adjusted, after rising 0.7 percent to A$10.24 billion in November, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In December 1995, retail sales rose 0.5 percent to A$10.05 billion.</p>
<p>In the December quarter, real retail sales at constant average 1989/90 prices fell 1.3 percent to A$25.56 billion seasonally adjusted, from the September quarter.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected retail sales to rise a median 0.5 percent in December and to fall 0.5 percent in the quarter.  </p>
<p>Australian retail sales, December (A$ billion)</p>
<p>			  Dec 96  Nov 96 mo/mo pct Dec 95  yr/yr pct</p>
<p>    Seasonally adj   10.13   10.24   -1.0    10.05     +0.8</p>
<p>    Unadjusted	 13.20   10.61  +24.4    13.22     -0.1</p>
<p>    Trend Estimate   10.14   10.17   -0.3    10.05     +0.9</p>
<p>Retail turnover by group percentage change, seasonally adj.</p>
<p>				Dec 96	 Nov 96	 Dec 95</p>
<p>Food retailing	     -2.0	   +0.4	   -1.2</p>
<p>Department stores	  +0.1	   +6.2	   +2.3</p>
<p>Clothing, soft goods     +0.4	   -0.3	   +0.9</p>
<p>Household goods	    -1.7	   -0.3	   +1.9</p>
<p>Recreational goods	 +7.7	   +0.6	   +8.4</p>
<p>Other retailing	    -1.6	   -0.2	   +0.4</p>
<p>Hospitality, services    -2.0	    0.0	   +0.1</p>
<p>Total			  -1.0	   +0.7	   +0.5</p>
</text>
